        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Powers of matrices are similar to powers of numbers. If <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A]</span> is a matrix, then <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A^n]</span> is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A]</span> multiplied by itself <span class=\"math\">[MATH: n]</span> times: \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: A^n = \\underbrace{A\\:\\cdot\\: A\\:\\cdot\\: \\ldots \\:\\cdot\\: A}_{\\Large{n\\text{ times}}}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Powers of matrices are similar to powers of numbers. If [MATH: A] is a matrix, then [MATH: A^n] is [MATH: A] multiplied by itself [MATH: n] times:\n[MATH: A^n = \\underbrace{A\\:\\cdot\\: A\\:\\cdot\\: \\ldots \\:\\cdot\\: A}_{\\Large{n\\text{ times}}}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A]</span> to be conformable with itself, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A]</span> needs to be a square matrix. So we can only take powers of square matrices.</p>",
            "readable_text": "For [MATH: A] to be conformable with itself, [MATH: A] needs to be a square matrix. So we can only take powers of square matrices.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To demonstrate, suppose that\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: [3|\u2212 1; 2|1]]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To demonstrate, suppose that\n[MATH: [3|\u2212 1; 2|1]]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Then we can calculate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A^2]</span> as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Then we can calculate [MATH: A^2] as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: A^{2}|= A \u22c5 A; = [3|\u2212 1; 2|1] \u22c5 [3|\u2212 1; 2|1]; = [3 \u22c5 3 + (\u2212 1) \u22c5 2|3 \u22c5 (\u2212 1) + (\u2212 1) \u22c5 1; 2 \u22c5 3 + 1 \u22c5 2|2 \u22c5 (\u2212 1) + 1 \u22c5 1]; = [7|\u2212 4; 8|\u2212 1]]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: A^{2}|= A \u22c5 A; = [3|\u2212 1; 2|1] \u22c5 [3|\u2212 1; 2|1]; = [3 \u22c5 3 + (\u2212 1) \u22c5 2|3 \u22c5 (\u2212 1) + (\u2212 1) \u22c5 1; 2 \u22c5 3 + 1 \u22c5 2|2 \u22c5 (\u2212 1) + 1 \u22c5 1]; = [7|\u2212 4; 8|\u2212 1]]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We say that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A^0 = I,]</span> the identity matrix of the same dimension as <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We say that [MATH: A^0 = I,] the identity matrix of the same dimension as [MATH: A.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nPowers of matrices are similar to powers of numbers. If [MATH: A] is a matrix, then [MATH: A^n] is [MATH: A] multiplied by itself [MATH: n] times:\n[MATH: A^n = \\underbrace{A\\:\\cdot\\: A\\:\\cdot\\: \\ldots \\:\\cdot\\: A}_{\\Large{n\\text{ times}}}]\n\nContent:\nFor [MATH: A] to be conformable with itself, [MATH: A] needs to be a square matrix. So we can only take powers of square matrices.\n\nContent:\nTo demonstrate, suppose that\n[MATH: [3|\u2212 1; 2|1]]\n\nContent:\nThen we can calculate [MATH: A^2] as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: A^{2}|= A \u22c5 A; = [3|\u2212 1; 2|1] \u22c5 [3|\u2212 1; 2|1]; = [3 \u22c5 3 + (\u2212 1) \u22c5 2|3 \u22c5 (\u2212 1) + (\u2212 1) \u22c5 1; 2 \u22c5 3 + 1 \u22c5 2|2 \u22c5 (\u2212 1) + 1 \u22c5 1]; = [7|\u2212 4; 8|\u2212 1]]\n\nContent:\nWe say that [MATH: A^0 = I,] the identity matrix of the same dimension as [MATH: A.]"
      },
