        "title": "Matrix Polynomials",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Now that we know how to compute powers of matrices, we can evaluate polynomials where the input is a square matrix. </p>",
            "readable_text": "Now that we know how to compute powers of matrices, we can evaluate polynomials where the input is a square matrix.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, consider the polynomial</p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, consider the polynomial",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(X) = X^2 + 4X + 3.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: f(X) = X^2 + 4X + 3.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Note that, in order to evaluate this polynomial for an input matrix <span class=\"math\">[MATH: X,]</span> we need to interpret any constants as multiples of the identity matrix. So, we interpret the polynomial as</p>",
            "readable_text": "Note that, in order to evaluate this polynomial for an input matrix [MATH: X,] we need to interpret any constants as multiples of the identity matrix. So, we interpret the polynomial as",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(X) = X^2 + 4X + 3I.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: f(X) = X^2 + 4X + 3I.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, if <span class=\"math\">[MATH: [1|1; 0|2]]</span> then</p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, if [MATH: [1|1; 0|2]] then",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: A^{2}|= [1|1; 0|2][1|1; 0|2]; = [1|3; 0|4],]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: A^{2}|= [1|1; 0|2][1|1; 0|2]; = [1|3; 0|4],]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>and we can evaluate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(A)]</span> as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "and we can evaluate [MATH: f(A)] as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(A)|= A^{2} + 4A + 3I; = [1|3; 0|4] + 4[1|1; 0|2] + 3[1|0; 0|1]; = [1|3; 0|4] + [4|4; 0|8] + [3|0; 0|3]; = [1 + 4 + 3|3 + 4 + 0; 0 + 0 + 0|4 + 8 + 3]; = [8|7; 0|15]]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: f(A)|= A^{2} + 4A + 3I; = [1|3; 0|4] + 4[1|1; 0|2] + 3[1|0; 0|1]; = [1|3; 0|4] + [4|4; 0|8] + [3|0; 0|3]; = [1 + 4 + 3|3 + 4 + 0; 0 + 0 + 0|4 + 8 + 3]; = [8|7; 0|15]]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
