            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(X)|= \u2212 X^{2} + 3X + 2; = \u2212 X^{2} + 3X + 2I]</span></p><p>So, we want to find <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(D)=-D^2+3D+2I.]</span></p><p>Let&#x27;s calculate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: D^2]</span> as follows:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: D^{2}|= D \u22c5 D; = [1|5; 0|\u2212 3] \u22c5 [1|5; 0|\u2212 3]; = [1|\u2212 10; 0|9]]</span></p><p>Now, we can evaluate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(D)\\mathbin{:}]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(D)|= \u2212 D^{2} + 3D + 2I; = \u2212 [1|\u2212 10; 0|9] + 3[1|5; 0|\u2212 3] + 2[1|0; 0|1]; = [\u2212 1|10; 0|\u2212 9] + [3|15; 0|\u2212 9] + [2|0; 0|2]; = [\u2212 1 + 3 + 2|10 + 15 + 0; 0|\u2212 9 \u2212 9 + 2]; = [4|25; 0|\u2212 16]]</span></p>",
