    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nPowers of matrices are similar to powers of numbers. If [MATH: A] is a matrix, then [MATH: A^n] is [MATH: A] multiplied by itself [MATH: n] times:\n[MATH: A^n = \\underbrace{A\\:\\cdot\\: A\\:\\cdot\\: \\ldots \\:\\cdot\\: A}_{\\Large{n\\text{ times}}}]\n\nContent:\nFor [MATH: A] to be conformable with itself, [MATH: A] needs to be a square matrix. So we can only take powers of square matrices.\n\nContent:\nTo demonstrate, suppose that\n[MATH: [3|\u2212 1; 2|1]]\n\nContent:\nThen we can calculate [MATH: A^2] as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: A^{2}|= A \u22c5 A; = [3|\u2212 1; 2|1] \u22c5 [3|\u2212 1; 2|1]; = [3 \u22c5 3 + (\u2212 1) \u22c5 2|3 \u22c5 (\u2212 1) + (\u2212 1) \u22c5 1; 2 \u22c5 3 + 1 \u22c5 2|2 \u22c5 (\u2212 1) + 1 \u22c5 1]; = [7|\u2212 4; 8|\u2212 1]]\n\nContent:\nWe say that [MATH: A^0 = I,] the identity matrix of the same dimension as [MATH: A.]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Finding a Power of a Matrix\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind [MATH: A^4] given that [MATH: [3|0; 5|\u2212 1]]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, to find [MATH: A^2,] we multiply [MATH: A] by itself:\n\n[MATH: A^{2}|= A \u22c5 A; = [3|0; 5|\u2212 1] \u22c5 [3|0; 5|\u2212 1]; = [9|0; 10|1]]\n\nNow, since [MATH: A^4 = A^2 \\cdot A^2,] we get\n\n[MATH: A^{4}|= A^{2} \u22c5 A^{2}; = [9|0; 10|1] \u22c5 [9|0; 10|1]; = [81|0; 100|1].]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: A = [3|2; \u2212 4|7]], then [MATH: A^{2} =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [1|20; \u2212 40|41]]\nb. [MATH: [17|20; \u2212 16|57]]\nc. [MATH: [9|4; 16|49]]\nd. [MATH: [0|0; 0|0]]\ne. [MATH: [3|2; \u2212 4|7]]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: A = [\u2212 1|\u2212 1; \u2212 2|1]], then [MATH: A^{4} =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [9|0; 0|9]]\nb. [MATH: [3|0; \u2212 3|9]]\nc. [MATH: [\u2212 9|\u2212 9; \u2212 18|9]]\nd. [MATH: [\u2212 1|\u2212 1; \u2212 2|1]]\ne. [MATH: [0|0; 0|0]]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Tutorial: Matrix Polynomials\n\nContent:\nNow that we know how to compute powers of matrices, we can evaluate polynomials where the input is a square matrix.\n\nContent:\nFor example, consider the polynomial\n\nContent:\n[MATH: f(X) = X^2 + 4X + 3.]\n\nContent:\nNote that, in order to evaluate this polynomial for an input matrix [MATH: X,] we need to interpret any constants as multiples of the identity matrix. So, we interpret the polynomial as\n\nContent:\n[MATH: f(X) = X^2 + 4X + 3I.]\n\nContent:\nFor example, if [MATH: [1|1; 0|2]] then\n\nContent:\n[MATH: A^{2}|= [1|1; 0|2][1|1; 0|2]; = [1|3; 0|4],]\n\nContent:\nand we can evaluate [MATH: f(A)] as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: f(A)|= A^{2} + 4A + 3I; = [1|3; 0|4] + 4[1|1; 0|2] + 3[1|0; 0|1]; = [1|3; 0|4] + [4|4; 0|8] + [3|0; 0|3]; = [1 + 4 + 3|3 + 4 + 0; 0 + 0 + 0|4 + 8 + 3]; = [8|7; 0|15]]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Example: Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial\n\nExample Prompt:\nConsider the matrix\n[MATH: [1|5; 0|\u2212 3]]\nFind [MATH: f(D)] if [MATH: f(X)=-X^2+3X+2.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n[MATH: f(X)|= \u2212 X^{2} + 3X + 2; = \u2212 X^{2} + 3X + 2I]\n\nSo, we want to find [MATH: f(D)=-D^2+3D+2I.]\n\nLet's calculate [MATH: D^2] as follows:\n[MATH: D^{2}|= D \u22c5 D; = [1|5; 0|\u2212 3] \u22c5 [1|5; 0|\u2212 3]; = [1|\u2212 10; 0|9]]\n\nNow, we can evaluate [MATH: f(D)\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: f(D)|= \u2212 D^{2} + 3D + 2I; = \u2212 [1|\u2212 10; 0|9] + 3[1|5; 0|\u2212 3] + 2[1|0; 0|1]; = [\u2212 1|10; 0|\u2212 9] + [3|15; 0|\u2212 9] + [2|0; 0|2]; = [\u2212 1 + 3 + 2|10 + 15 + 0; 0|\u2212 9 \u2212 9 + 2]; = [4|25; 0|\u2212 16]]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nConsider the matrix [MATH: C = [1|2; 3|1].] Find [MATH: f(C)] if [MATH: f(X) = X^{2} \u2212 2X \u2212 5.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [\u2212 1|\u2212 2; \u2212 3|\u2212 1]]\nb. [MATH: [7|4; 6|7]]\nc. [MATH: [0|0; 0|0]]\nd. [MATH: [7|\u2212 2; \u2212 3|7]]\ne. [MATH: [\u2212 1|4; 6|\u2212 1]]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nConsider the matrix [MATH: A = [1|\u2212 3; 4|0].] Find [MATH: f(A)] if [MATH: f(X) = X^{2} + 2X \u2212 3.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [12|6; \u2212 9|\u2212 5]]\nb. [MATH: [2|\u2212 5; 12|\u2212 3]]\nc. [MATH: [\u2212 15|12; 12|\u2212 15]]\nd. [MATH: [\u2212 12|\u2212 7; 12|5]]\ne. [MATH: [\u2212 12|\u2212 9; 12|\u2212 15]]"
